{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784692203281,"sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_US1SGQbDulGYzT9QlsJwUj2m","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/review/lineages/sol-high/deep-review-strategy.md","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/review/lineages/sol-high/deep-review-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Review Strategy: Compiled-Routing Coverage Build-Out\n2: \n3: ## Topic\n4: Review the completed compiled-routing coverage build-out and default-on cutover against its canonical packet, six implementation commits, routing runtime, parity harness, and lockstep documentation surfaces.\n5: \n6: ## Review Dimensions\n7: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n8: - [ ] D1 Correctness\n9: - [ ] D2 Security\n10: - [ ] D3 Traceability\n11: - [ ] D4 Maintainability\n12: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n13: \n14: ## Non-Goals\n15: - Do not modify implementation or canonical packet documents.\n16: - Do not review unrelated worktree changes or the operator-gated merge.\n17: - Do not substitute prose claims for direct implementation, test, or commit evidence.\n18: \n19: ## Stop Conditions\n20: - Run exactly 10 iterations. Convergence before iteration 10 is telemetry only.\n21: - Stop at the hard ceiling with `maxIterationsReached`, preserving failed gates as evidence.\n22: \n23: ## Completed Dimensions\n24: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n25: None yet.\n26: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n27: \n28: ## Running Findings\n29: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n30: - P0: 0 active\n31: - P1: 1 active\n32: - P2: 0 active\n33: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n34: \n35: ## What Worked\n36: - Commit-bounded scope discovery identified concrete producer, consumer, test, manifest, and documentation surfaces before review.\n37: - Direct producer/test comparison exposed the refresh race without relying on speculative caller behavior (iteration 1).\n38: \n39: ## What Failed\n40: - Spec Memory trigger retrieval was unavailable (`Not connected`); canonical packet continuity and direct repository evidence are the fallback.\n41: \n42: ## Exhausted Approaches\n43: - None yet.\n44: \n45: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n46: - Completed pivots: 0\n47: - Failed pivots: 0\n48: - Audited overrides: 0\n49: - Swept: none yet\n50: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n51: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n52: \n53: ## Ruled Out Directions\n54: - No review of unrelated dirty paths outside the target and lineage packet.\n55: - Compile-failure partial writes and CLI exit-code inversion are ruled out for the manifest refresh path (iteration 1).\n56: \n57: ## Next Focus\n58: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n59: - Dimension: correctness\n60: - Focus area: compiled router scoring, selection, and parity-classification semantics\n61: - Reason: verify the six-commit behavioral claims against the actual producers and tests\n62: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n63: \n64: ## Known Context\n65: - Target packet claims all seven hubs are `compiled-serving`, default-on, reversible, and frozen-scorer clean.\n66: - Six commits define the implementation range: `f19ee17179`, `e56361ee53`, `f9f639674b`, `b03b1dd882`, `6ba5f2957f`, `7dfffa0c93`.\n67: - Canonical continuity is contradictory: `spec.md`, `checklist.md`, and `implementation-summary.md` claim completion, while `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `decision-record.md` retain planned or blocked metadata and unchecked work.\n68: - `resource-map.md` is absent, so the resource-map coverage gate is skipped.\n69: \n70: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n71: - Target pointers: the 34 files listed in `deep-review-config.json`, bounded to implementation, tests, runtime consumers, lockstep skill/template surfaces, and canonical packet docs.\n72: - Behavior claims: compiled routes equal legacy for all seven hubs; kill-switch and cohort removal restore legacy; manifest refresh fails closed; frozen scorer files remain unchanged.\n73: - Reuse and conventions: sk-design router is the reference implementation; parity is measured by the route-gold harness; compiled decisions must not exceed legacy targets.\n74: - Risks and gaps: completion-metadata drift, harness-vs-routing attribution, default-on cohort duplication, stale evidence, and absent full seven-hub LUNA-HIGH acceptance.\n75: \n76: ## Cross-Reference Status\n77: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n78: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n79: |---|---|---|---:|---|\n80: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | Normative claims require direct implementation evidence. |\n81: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | Checked claims require current evidence. |\n82: | `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | - | Target is a spec folder. |\n83: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | - | Target is a spec folder. |\n84: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | Default-on catalog wording is in scope. |\n85: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | Acceptance and route-gold capability claims are in scope. |\n86: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n87: \n88: ## Files Under Review\n89: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n90: Scope is the ordered `reviewScopeFiles` list in `deep-review-config.json` (34 files). Coverage begins at 0/34.\n91: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n92: \n93: ## Review Boundaries\n94: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n95: - Max iterations: 10\n96: - Stop policy: max-iterations\n97: - Convergence threshold: 0.10\n98: - Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n99: - Session: `fanout-sol-high-1784691838667-iv78vk`, generation 1, lineage `new`\n100: - Artifact root: `review/lineages/sol-high`\n101: - Resource-map coverage: skipped (source map absent at init)\n102: - Target files: read-only\n103: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n104: \n105: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n106: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n107: - [ ] security\n108: - [ ] traceability\n109: - [ ] maintainability\n110: \n111: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n112: \n113: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n114: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n115: - [x] correctness\n116: \n117: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n118: \n119: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n120: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n121: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n122: - P1 (Required): 1\n123: - P2 (Suggestions): 0\n124: - Resolved: 0\n125: \n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n127: \n128: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n129: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n130: ### `checklist_evidence`: not executed in this iteration. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n131: - What was tried: `checklist_evidence`: not executed in this iteration.\n132: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n133: - Do NOT retry: `checklist_evidence`: not executed in this iteration.\n134: \n135: ### `spec_code`: partial; the fail-closed and field-preservation claims hold for sequential execution, but concurrent preservation is not demonstrated. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n136: - What was tried: `spec_code`: partial; the fail-closed and field-preservation claims hold for sequential execution, but concurrent preservation is not demonstrated.\n137: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n138: - Do NOT retry: `spec_code`: partial; the fail-closed and field-preservation claims hold for sequential execution, but concurrent preservation is not demonstrated.\n139: \n140: ### CLI exit-code inversion: ruled out by direct branch and test review. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:63-77] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n141: - What was tried: CLI exit-code inversion: ruled out by direct branch and test review. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:63-77]\n142: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n143: - Do NOT retry: CLI exit-code inversion: ruled out by direct branch and test review. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:63-77]\n144: \n145: ### Partial write caused by compile failure: ruled out because compilation precedes the write. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:565-590] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n146: - What was tried: Partial write caused by compile failure: ruled out because compilation precedes the write. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:565-590]\n147: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n148: - Do NOT retry: Partial write caused by compile failure: ruled out because compilation precedes the write. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:565-590]\n149: \n150: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n151: \n152: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n153: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n154: - Dimension: correctness - Focus area: compiled router scoring, selection, and parity-classification semantics - Reason: verify that the six-commit behavioral claims match implementation - Rotation status: broaden within correctness before security - Blocked/productive carry-forward: manifest refresh race remains active; path validation is exhausted - Required evidence: router and parity-harness producer/consumer traces Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n155: \n156: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n(End of file - total 156 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deep Review Strategy: Compiled-Routing Coverage Build-Out\n\n## Topic\nReview the completed compiled-routing coverage build-out and default-on cutover against its canonical packet, six implementation commits, routing runtime, parity harness, and lockstep documentation surfaces.\n\n## Review Dimensions\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness\n- [ ] D2 Security\n- [ ] D3 Traceability\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## Non-Goals\n- Do not modify implementation or canonical packet documents.\n- Do not review unrelated worktree changes or the operator-gated merge.\n- Do not substitute prose claims for direct implementation, test, or commit evidence.\n\n## Stop Conditions\n- Run exactly 10 iterations. Convergence before iteration 10 is telemetry only.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/review/lineages/sol-high/deep-review-strategy.md","text":"# Deep Review Strategy: Compiled-Routing Coverage Build-Out\n\n## Topic\nReview the completed compiled-routing coverage build-out and default-on cutover against its canonical packet, six implementation commits, routing runtime, parity harness, and lockstep documentation surfaces.\n\n## Review Dimensions\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness\n- [ ] D2 Security\n- [ ] D3 Traceability\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## Non-Goals\n- Do not modify implementation or canonical packet documents.\n- Do not review unrelated worktree changes or the operator-gated merge.\n- Do not substitute prose claims for direct implementation, test, or commit evidence.\n\n## Stop Conditions\n- Run exactly 10 iterations. Convergence before iteration 10 is telemetry only.\n- Stop at the hard ceiling with `maxIterationsReached`, preserving failed gates as evidence.\n\n## Completed Dimensions\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\nNone yet.\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## Running Findings\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- P0: 0 active\n- P1: 1 active\n- P2: 0 active\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## What Worked\n- Commit-bounded scope discovery identified concrete producer, consumer, test, manifest, and documentation surfaces before review.\n- Direct producer/test comparison exposed the refresh race without relying on speculative caller behavior (iteration 1).\n\n## What Failed\n- Spec Memory trigger retrieval was unavailable (`Not connected`); canonical packet continuity and direct repository evidence are the fallback.\n\n## Exhausted Approaches\n- None yet.\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n## Ruled Out Directions\n- No review of unrelated dirty paths outside the target and lineage packet.\n- Compile-failure partial writes and CLI exit-code inversion are ruled out for the manifest refresh path (iteration 1).\n\n## Next Focus\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: compiled router scoring, selection, and parity-classification semantics\n- Reason: verify the six-commit behavioral claims against the actual producers and tests\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## Known Context\n- Target packet claims all seven hubs are `compiled-serving`, default-on, reversible, and frozen-scorer clean.\n- Six commits define the implementation range: `f19ee17179`, `e56361ee53`, `f9f639674b`, `b03b1dd882`, `6ba5f2957f`, `7dfffa0c93`.\n- Canonical continuity is contradictory: `spec.md`, `checklist.md`, and `implementation-summary.md` claim completion, while `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `decision-record.md` retain planned or blocked metadata and unchecked work.\n- `resource-map.md` is absent, so the resource-map coverage gate is skipped.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n- Target pointers: the 34 files listed in `deep-review-config.json`, bounded to implementation, tests, runtime consumers, lockstep skill/template surfaces, and canonical packet docs.\n- Behavior claims: compiled routes equal legacy for all seven hubs; kill-switch and cohort removal restore legacy; manifest refresh fails closed; frozen scorer files remain unchanged.\n- Reuse and conventions: sk-design router is the reference implementation; parity is measured by the route-gold harness; compiled decisions must not exceed legacy targets.\n- Risks and gaps: completion-metadata drift, harness-vs-routing attribution, default-on cohort duplication, stale evidence, and absent full seven-hub LUNA-HIGH acceptance.\n\n## Cross-Reference Status\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | Normative claims require direct implementation evidence. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | Checked claims require current evidence. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | - | Target is a spec folder. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | - | Target is a spec folder. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | Default-on catalog wording is in scope. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | Acceptance and route-gold capability claims are in scope. |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## Files Under Review\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\nScope is the ordered `reviewScopeFiles` list in `deep-review-config.json` (34 files). Coverage begins at 0/34.\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## Review Boundaries\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: 10\n- Stop policy: max-iterations\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n- Session: `fanout-sol-high-1784691838667-iv78vk`, generation 1, lineage `new`\n- Artifact root: `review/lineages/sol-high`\n- Resource-map coverage: skipped (source map absent at init)\n- Target files: read-only\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] security\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 1\n- P2 (Suggestions): 0\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n### `checklist_evidence`: not executed in this iteration. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n- What was tried: `checklist_evidence`: not executed in this iteration.\n- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n- Do NOT retry: `checklist_evidence`: not executed in this iteration.\n\n### `spec_code`: partial; the fail-closed and field-preservation claims hold for sequential execution, but concurrent preservation is not demonstrated. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n- What was tried: `spec_code`: partial; the fail-closed and field-preservation claims hold for sequential execution, but concurrent preservation is not demonstrated.\n- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n- Do NOT retry: `spec_code`: partial; the fail-closed and field-preservation claims hold for sequential execution, but concurrent preservation is not demonstrated.\n\n### CLI exit-code inversion: ruled out by direct branch and test review. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:63-77] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n- What was tried: CLI exit-code inversion: ruled out by direct branch and test review. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:63-77]\n- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n- Do N