:\"Live all-hub flag-off replay supports the fleet kill-switch claim.\"}]},\"newFindingsRatio\":0.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Stabilization replay confirmed release controls and found no new defect.\",\"ruledOut\":[\"F006 affecting live routing\",\"partial-cohort kill-switch coverage\"],\"budgetProfile\":\"verify\",\"sessionId\":... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"claim_adjudication\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":9,\"passed\":true,\"activeP0P1\":5,\"missingPackets\":[],\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-22T04:49:01.000Z\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-sol-high-1784691838667-iv78vk\",\"generation\":1}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":28,"totalLines":28,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/review/lineages/sol-high/deep-review-state.jsonl","time":{"start":1784694378448,"end":1784694378485}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_09d4e0459806ebcf016a60466a531c8191985078c1d44ae688"}},"id":"prt_f88130fca001uno2VZxpXddlrc","sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","messageID":"msg_f8812e18c001KheHCKVwDav21Z"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784694378525,"sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_G6zbj2ffBwcLycRrWpe5gQCT","state":{"status":"error","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/reduce-state.cjs","offset":1,"limit":240},"error":"File not found: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/reduce-state.cjs","time":{"start":1784694378512,"end":1784694378518}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_09d4e0459806ebcf016a60466a53308191a67ed0a8b8b482b0"}},"id":"prt_f88130ffb001vYe3HCuM2MJSeu","sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","messageID":"msg_f8812e18c001KheHCKVwDav21Z"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784694378525,"sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_AOfV9p4NLqHvmAmUFPSXSU8U","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/completion-criteria.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/completion-criteria.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Completion Criteria\n3: description: Full definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop -- loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates that must pass before STOP, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"review loop completion criteria\"\n6:   - \"review success criteria\"\n7:   - \"review definition of done\"\n8:   - \"review release readiness validation\"\n9: importance_tier: important\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 1.11.0.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Completion Criteria\n15: \n16: Full definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop: loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates STOP must clear, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: This reference is the authoritative checklist for \"is this review loop actually done.\" SKILL.md §6 SUCCESS CRITERIA carries a condensed summary and links here for the full enumeration; use this file when verifying a completed run, debugging a premature STOP, or reconciling completion metadata against the loop's real state.\n25: \n26: ### When to Use\n27: \n28: - Verifying a review loop's completion before accepting its verdict.\n29: - Debugging why STOP was blocked or why synthesis produced an incomplete report.\n30: - Reconciling `review-report.md` claims against the canonical state files.\n31: - Auditing a run for the release-readiness handoff.\n32: \n33: ### Relationship to `loop-state-and-gates.md`\n34: \n35: `references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md` defines the three state-machine-level binary gates (Evidence, Scope, Coverage) that block a STOP *decision* inside the convergence check. This file is the broader definition-of-done: it also covers artifact existence, report structure, severity-field completeness, and the release-readiness handoff -- checked once the loop believes it has already reached STOP.\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 2. LOOP COMPLETION\n40: \n41: A review loop is considered complete when every item below holds:\n42: \n43: - The loop reached convergence (composite stop score above `compositeStopScore`, with required gates green) OR hit `maxIterations` without false-positive STOP.\n44: - Every configured review dimension has at least one full iteration of coverage recorded in `deep-review-state.jsonl` and reflected in `deep-review-strategy.md`.\n45: - Required traceability protocols (`spec_code`, `checklist_evidence`) executed at least once. Overlay protocols that apply to the target type ran or were explicitly marked N/A.\n46: - All canonical state files exist and parse cleanly: `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, and one `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` per dispatched iteration.\n47: - `review/resource-map.md` was emitted from converged delta evidence unless `config.resource_map.emit == false` (operator flag `--no-resource-map`).\n48: - `review/review-report.md` carries all 9 core sections (Executive Summary, Planning Trigger, Active Finding Registry, Remediation Workstreams, Spec Seed, Plan Seed, Traceability Status, Deferred Items, Audit Appendix) plus the conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` section when `resource_map_present == true`.\n49: - Canonical continuity surfaces updated via `generate-context.js` (description.json, graph-metadata.json, indexed memory entries).\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. QUALITY GATES\n54: \n55: Each gate is binary: pass or block. STOP cannot be legal until every gate passes.\n56: \n57: - **Config validity**: `deep-review-config.json` parses, names every required field, and lineage block matches the current run (`sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`, `continuedFromRun`, `releaseReadinessState`).\n58: - **Strategy initialization**: `deep-review-strategy.md` carries the Files Under Review table, Cross-Reference Status grouped by core vs overlay, Known Context, and Review Boundaries.\n59: - **State consistency**: `deep-review-state.jsonl` opens with the config record and appends one iteration record per dispatched iteration. Reducer-owned fields in `deep-review-findings-registry.json` reconcile against JSONL totals.\n60: - **Iteration completeness**: every dispatched iteration produced both an `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` (non-empty, ending with the canonical `Review verdict: PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL` line) AND a JSONL delta record with `findingDetails[]`, `findingsSummary`, `newFindingsRatio`.\n61: - **Severity coverage**: every reported finding carries `severity` in {P0, P1, P2}, `category`, `file:line` evidence, `finding_class`, and a `content_hash` for synthesis dedup.\n62: - **Advisory numeric score**: `riskScore` may appear in finding details as non-gating context only; verdict logic must ignore it.\n63: - **Adversarial replay**: every P0 finding survived adversarial self-check. Rejected P0s downgraded with rationale recorded in the iteration narrative.\n64: - **Coverage threshold**: `dimensions_covered_count == configured_dimensions_count` AND required traceability protocols covered, stable for at least `minStabilizationPasses` iterations.\n65: - **Acceptance coverage**: when the spec-folder lifecycle predicate is active, the final report records `AC_COVERAGE` status, covered/total, floor, and next action; default-off INFO output is advisory and does not by itself block STOP.\n66: - **Security-sensitive override**: when the run targets security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, or shared policy, the gates from `references/convergence/convergence.md` \"Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides\" apply (`minStabilizationPasses=2`, closed-finding replay required, fix-completeness gate enforced).\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 4. VALIDATION SUCCESS\n71: \n72: The release-readiness handoff is valid when:\n73: \n74: - The final report records stop reason, iteration count, dimension coverage, severity counts (P0/P1/P2), verdict (PASS / CONDITIONAL / FAIL), and release-readiness state (`in-progress`, `converged`, `release-blocking`).\n75: - Verdict logic matches: PASS = no P0/P1 findings (P2 advisories permitted with `hasAdvisories: true`). CONDITIONAL = P1 findings present with remediation plan. FAIL = any P0 confirmed after adversarial self-check.\n76: - `resource-map.md` Phase-5 Augmentation section (if present) lists novel logic gaps with iteration source links, or explicitly records the empty-result case.\n77: - `skill_advisor.py \"run a deep review loop\" --threshold 0.8` still surfaces the skill after any graph-metadata edits.\n78: - `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict` exits 0 on the target spec folder.\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 5. RELATED RESOURCES\n83: \n84: - `references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md` -- state transitions, error handling, and the Evidence/Scope/Coverage STOP-decision gates.\n85: - `references/state/state-outputs.md` -- packet file ownership and the `review-report.md` section list.\n86: - `references/state/state-format.md` -- schemas for every state file referenced above.\n87: - `references/convergence/convergence.md` -- composite stop score, `minStabilizationPasses`, and Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides.\n\n(End of file - total 87 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Completion Criteria\ndescription: Full definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop -- loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates that must pass before STOP, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"review loop completion criteria\"\n  - \"review success criteria\"\n  - \"review definition of done\"\n  - \"review release readiness validation\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review Completion Criteria\n\nFull definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop: loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates STOP must clear, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/completion-criteria.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Completion Criteria\ndescription: Full definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop -- loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates that must pass before STOP, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"review loop completion criteria\"\n  - \"review success criteria\"\n  - \"review definition of done\"\n  - \"review release readiness validation\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review Completion Criteria\n\nFull definition-of-done checklist for a deep-review loop: loop completion conditions, the binary quality gates STOP must clear, and release-readiness validation success criteria.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nThis reference is the authoritative checklist for \"is this review loop actually done.\" SKILL.md §6 SUCCESS CRITERIA carries a condensed summary and links here for the full enumeration; use this file when verifying a completed run, debugging a premature STOP, or reconciling completion metadata against the loop's real state.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Verifying a review loop's completion before accepting its verdict.\n- Debugging why STOP was blocked or why synthesis produced an incomplete report.\n- Reconciling `review-report.md` claims against the canonical state files.\n- Auditing a run for the release-readiness handoff.\n\n### Relationship to `loop-state-and-gates.md`\n\n`references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md` defines the three state-machine-level binary gates (Evidence, Scope, Coverage) that block a STOP *decision* inside the convergence check. This file is the broader definition-of-done: it also covers artifact existence, report structure, severity-field completeness, and the release-readiness handoff -- checked once the loop believes it has already reached STOP.\n\n---\n\n## 2. LOOP COMPLETION\n\nA review loop is considered complete when every item below holds:\n\n- The loop reached convergence (composite stop score above `compositeStopScore`, with required gates green) OR hit `maxIterations` without false-positive STOP.\n- Every configured review dimension has at least one full iteration of coverage recorded in `deep-review-state.jsonl` and reflected in `deep-review-strategy.md`.\n- Required traceability protocols (`spec_code`, `checklist_evidence`) executed at least once. Overlay protocols that apply to the target type ran or were explicitly marked N/A.\n- All canonical state files exist and parse cleanly: `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-strategy.md`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, and one `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` per dispatched iteration.\n- `review/resource-map.md` was emitted from converged delta evidence unless `config.resource_map.emit == false` (operator flag `--no-resource-map`).\n- `review/review-report.md` carries all 9 core sections (Executive Summary, Planning Trigger, Active Finding Registry, Remediation Workstreams, Spec Seed, Plan Seed, Traceability Status, Deferred Items, Audit Appendix) plus the conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` section when `resource_map_present == true`.\n- Canonical continuity surfaces updated via `generate-context.js` (description.json, graph-metadata.json, indexed memory entries).\n\n---\n\n## 3. QUALITY GATES\n\nEach gate is binary: pass or block. STOP cannot be legal until every gate passes.\n\n- **Config validity**: `deep-review-config.json` parses, names every required field, and lineage block matches the current run (`sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`, `continuedFromRun`, `releaseReadinessState`).\n- **Strategy initialization**: `deep-review-strategy.md` carries the Files Under Review table, Cross-Reference Status grouped by core vs overlay, Known Context, and Review Boundaries.\n- **State consistency**: `deep-review-state.jsonl` opens with the config record and appends one iteration record per dispatched iteration. Reducer-owned fields in `deep-review-findings-registry.json` reconcile against JSONL totals.\n- **Iteration completeness**: every dispatched iteration produced both an `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` (non-empty, ending with the canonical `Review verdict: PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL` line) AND a JSONL delta record with `findingDetails[]`, `findingsSummary`, `newFindingsRatio`.\n- **Severity coverage**: every reported finding carries `severity` in {P0, P1, P2}, `category`, `file:line` evidence, `finding_class`, and a `content_hash` for synthesis dedup.\n- **Advisory numeric score**: `riskScore` may appear in finding details as non-gating context only; verdict logic must ignore it.\n- **Adversarial replay**: every P0 finding survived adversarial self-check. Rejected P0s downgraded with rationale recorded in the iteration narrative.\n- **Coverage threshold**: `dimensions_covered_count == configured_dimensions_count` AND required traceability protocols covered, stable for at least `minStabilizationPasses` iterations.\n- **Acceptance coverage**: when the spec-folder lifecycle predicate is active, the final report records `AC_COVERAGE` status, covered/total, floor, and next action; default-off INFO output is advisory and does not by itself block STOP.\n- **Security-sensitive override**: when the run targets security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, or shared policy, the gates from `references/convergence/convergence.md` \"Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides\" apply (`minStabilizationPasses=2`, closed-finding replay required, fix-completeness gate enforced).\n\n---\n\n## 4. VALIDATION SUCCESS\n\nThe release-readiness handoff is valid when:\n\n- The final report records stop reason, iteration count, dimension coverage, severity counts (P0/P1/P2), verdict (PASS / CONDITIONAL / FAIL), and release-readiness state (`in-progress`, `converged`, `release-blocking`).\n- Verdict logic matches: PASS = no P0/P1 findings (P2 advisories permitted with `hasAdvisories: true`). CONDITIONAL = P1 findings present with remediation plan. FAIL = any P0 confirmed after adversarial self-check.\n- `resource-map.md` Phase-5 Augmentation section (if present) lists novel logic gaps with iteration source links, or explicitly records the empty-result case.\n- `skill_advisor.py \"run a deep review loop\" --threshold 0.8` still surfaces the skill after any graph-metadata edits.\n- `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict` exits 0 on the target spec folder.\n\n---\n\n## 5. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- `references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md` -- state transitions, error handling, and the Evidence/Scope/Coverage STOP-decision gates.\n- `references/state/state-outputs.md` -- packet file ownership and the `review-report.md` section list.\n- `references/state/state-format.md` -- schemas for every state file referenced above.\n- `references/convergence/convergence.md` -- composite stop score, `minStabilizationPasses`, and Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":87,"totalLines":87,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/completion-criteria.md","time":{"start":1784694378464,"end":1784694378521}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_09d4e0459806ebcf016a60466a5324819195a26f0ef0937e7e"}},"id":"prt_f88130fd2001MG9TFqQNmdx0DB","sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","messageID":"msg_f8812e18c001KheHCKVwDav21Z"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784694378535,"sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_3st0s18X6V6EJK5DW3Vi6tnY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-outputs.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-outputs.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Deep Review State Outputs\"\n3: description: \"Focused reference for deep-review packet files, markdown outputs, reducer-owned views, and synthesis artifacts.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state outputs\"\n6:   - \"review packet outputs\"\n7:   - \"review dashboard output\"\n8:   - \"review report output\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 1.11.0.3\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review State Outputs\n15: \n16: This reference explains the files operators read during and after a review loop. Use `references/state/state-format.md` for schemas and field-level contracts.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: Deep-review outputs are audit artifacts. Iteration agents write evidence, the reducer writes derived state, and synthesis writes the release-readiness report.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. PACKET FILES\n27: \n28: | File | Owner | Mutability | Purpose |\n29: |------|-------|------------|---------|\n30: | `deep-review-config.json` | Workflow | Immutable after init | Run parameters, lineage, threshold settings |\n31: | `deep-review-state.jsonl` | Workflow and iteration contract | Append-only | Config, iteration, blocked-stop, pause, synthesis events |\n32: | `deep-review-findings-registry.json` | Reducer | Regenerated | Active, resolved, repeated, and blocked findings |\n33: | `deep-review-strategy.md` | Reducer with operator-readable sections | Regenerated/updated | Dimension order, known context, next focus |\n34: | `deep-review-dashboard.md` | Reducer | Regenerated | Current status, trend, verdict preview |\n35: | `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` | Iteration agent | Write-once | Detailed findings for one pass |\n36: | `review-report.md` | Synthesis | Final output | Findings-first release-readiness report |\n37: | `resource-map.md` | Synthesis | Final or disabled | Converged delta evidence map |\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 3. ITERATION MARKDOWN\n42: \n43: Each iteration file must be non-empty and end with exactly one final verdict line:\n44: \n45: ```text\n46: Review verdict: PASS\n47: ```\n48: \n49: ```text\n50: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n51: ```\n52: \n53: ```text\n54: Review verdict: FAIL\n55: ```\n56: \n57: The line maps to the findings in that iteration only. Synthesis computes the final release verdict from the full state.\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: ## 4. DASHBOARD\n62: \n63: The dashboard is a status view, not the source of truth. It should display:\n64: \n65: - Current iteration and next focus.\n66: - Active P0/P1/P2 counts.\n67: - Dimension coverage.\n68: - Convergence trend.\n69: - Gate blockers.\n70: - Provisional verdict.\n71: \n72: If dashboard data disagrees with JSONL, JSONL wins and the reducer must regenerate the dashboard.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ## 5. FINAL REPORT\n77: \n78: `review-report.md` is the handoff artifact. It carries:\n79: \n80: - Executive summary.\n81: - Planning trigger.\n82: - Active finding registry.\n83: - Remediation workstreams.\n84: - Spec seed.\n85: - Plan seed.\n86: - Traceability status.\n87: - Deferred items.\n88: - Audit appendix.\n89: - Optional Resource Map Coverage Gate section when a map existed at init.\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n94: \n95: - `references/state/state-format.md` for schemas.\n96: - `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md` for reducer ownership.\n97: - `references/convergence/convergence-signals.md` for STOP fields shown in dashboard/report.\n\n(End of file - total 97 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Review State Outputs\"\ndescription: \"Focused reference for deep-review packet files, markdown outputs, reducer-owned views, and synthesis artifacts.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review state outputs\"\n  - \"review packet outputs\"\n  - \"review dashboard output\"\n  - \"review report output\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Review State Outputs\n\nThis reference explains the files operators read during and after a review loop. Use `references/state/state-format.md` for schemas and field-level contracts.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-outputs.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Review State Outputs\"\ndescription: \"Focused reference for deep-review packet files, markdown outputs, reducer-owned views, and synthesis artifacts.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review state outputs\"\n  - \"review packet outputs\"\n  - \"review dashboard output\"\n  - \"review report output\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Review State Outputs\n\nThis reference explains the files operators read during and after a review loop. Use `references/state/state-format.md` for schemas and field-level contracts.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nDeep-review outputs are audit artifacts. Iteration agents write evidence, the reducer writes derived state, and synthesis writes the release-readiness report.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PACKET FILES\n\n| File | Owner | Mutability | Purpose |\n|------|-------|------------|---------|\n| `deep-review-config.json` | Workflow | Immutable after init | Run parameters, lineage, threshold settings |\n| `deep-review-state.jsonl` | Workflow and iteration contract | Append-only | Config, iteration, blocked-stop, pause, synthesis events |\n| `deep-review-findings-registry.json` | Reducer | Regenerated | Active, resolved, repeated, and blocked findings |\n| `deep-review-strategy.md` | Reducer with operator-readable sections | Regenerated/updated | Dimension order, known context, next focus |\n| `deep-review-dashboard.md` | Reducer | Regenerated | Current status, trend, verdict preview |\n| `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` | Iteration agent | Write-once | Detailed findings for one pass |\n| `review-report.md` | Synthesis | Final output | Findings-first release-readiness report |\n| `resource-map.md` | Synthesis | Final or disabled | Converged delta evidence map |\n\n---\n\n## 3. ITERATION MARKDOWN\n\nEach iteration file must be non-empty and end with exactly one final verdict line:\n\n```text\nReview verdict: PASS\n```\n\n```text\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n```\n\n```text\nReview verdict: FAIL\n```\n\nThe line maps to the findings in that iteration only. Synthesis computes the final release verdict from the full state.\n\n---\n\n## 4. DASHBOARD\n\nThe dashboard is a status view, not the source of truth. It should display:\n\n- Current iteration and next focus.\n- Active P0/P1/P2 counts.\n- Dimension coverage.\n- Convergence trend.\n- Gate blockers.\n- Provisional verdict.\n\nIf dashboard data disagrees with JSONL, JSONL wins and the reducer must regenerate the dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## 5. FINAL REPORT\n\n`review-report.md` is the handoff artifact. It carries:\n\n- Executive summary.\n- Planning trigger.\n- Active finding registry.\n- Remediation workstreams.\n- Spec seed.\n- Plan seed.\n- Traceability status.\n- Deferred items.\n- Audit appendix.\n- Optional Resource Map Coverage Gate section when a map existed at init.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- `references/state/state-format.md` for schemas.\n- `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md` for reducer ownership.\n- `references/convergence/convergence-signals.md` for STOP fields shown in dashboard/report.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":97,"totalLines":97,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-outputs.md","time":{"start":1784694378489,"end":1784694378533}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_09d4e0459806ebcf016a60466a53288191b85d1f7f14f9242d"}},"id":"prt_f88130fef001OjhlujZOQ435RS","sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","messageID":"msg_f8812e18c001KheHCKVwDav21Z"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1784694379143,"sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","part":{"id":"prt_f8813127c001vhbzXRvjvRf8HJ","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"a397e926b1c978ccbe2889409bb61786ac43b14c","messageID":"msg_f8812e18c001KheHCKVwDav21Z","sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":45307,"input":7373,"output":520,"reasoning":38,"cache":{"write":0,"read":37376}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1784694382257,"sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","part":{"id":"prt_f88131eaa001RBKwuAyN9KbFaY","messageID":"msg_f88131454001PVpOd9dZ5tcGLO","sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","snapshot":"a397e926b1c978ccbe2889409bb61786ac43b14c","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784694393525,"sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_KpdiTfgmSOUF5C6VgzqcZR5Q","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/review/lineages/sol-high/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/review/lineages/sol-high/deep-review-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Review Strategy: Compiled-Routing Coverage Build-Out\n2: \n3: ## Topic\n4: Review the completed compiled-routing coverage build-out and default-on cutover against its canonical packet, six implementation commits, routing runtime, parity harness, and lockstep documentation surfaces.\n5: \n6: ## Review Dimensions\n7: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n8: - [ ] D1 Correctness\n9: - [ ] D2 Security\n10: - [ ] D3 Traceability\n11: - [ ] D4 Maintainability\n12: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n13: \n14: ## Non-Goals\n15: - Do not modify implementation or canonical packet documents.\n16: - Do not review unrelated worktree changes or the operator-gated merge.\n17: - Do not substitute prose claims for direct implementation, test, or commit evidence.\n18: \n19: ## Stop Conditions\n20: - Run exactly 10 iterations. Convergence before iteration 10 is telemetry only.\n21: - Stop at the hard ceiling with `maxIterationsReached`, preserving failed gates as evidence.\n22: \n23: ## Completed Dimensions\n24: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n25: None yet.\n26: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n27: \n28: ## Running Findings\n29: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n30: - P0: 0 active\n31: - P1: 1 active\n32: - P2: 0 active\n33: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n34: \n35: ## What Worked\n36: - Commit-bounded scope discovery identified concrete producer, consumer, test, manifest, and documentation surfaces before review.\n37: - Direct producer/test comparison exposed the refresh race without relying on speculative caller behavior (iteration 1).\n38: \n39: ## What Failed\n40: - Spec Memory trigger retrieval was unavailable (`Not connected`); canonical packet continuity and direct repository evidence are the fallback.\n41: \n42: ## Exhausted Approaches\n43: - None yet.\n44: \n45: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n46: - Completed pivots: 0\n47: - Failed pivots: 0\n48: - Audited overrides: 0\n49: - Swept: none yet\n50: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n51: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n52: \n53: ## Ruled Out Directions\n54: - No review of unrelated dirty paths outside the target and lineage packet.\n55: - Compile-failure partial writes and CLI exit-code inversion are ruled out for the manifest refresh path (iteration 1).\n56: \n57: ## Next Focus\n58: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n59: - Dimension: correctness\n60: - Focus area: compiled router scoring, selection, and parity-classification semantics\n61: - Reason: verify the six-commit behavioral claims against the actual producers and tests\n62: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n63: \n64: ## Known Context\n65: - Target packet claims all seven hubs are `compiled-serving`, default-on, reversible, and frozen-scorer clean.\n66: - Six commits define the implementation range: `f19ee17179`, `e56361ee53`, `f9f639674b`, `b03b1dd882`, `6ba5f2957f`, `7dfffa0c93`.\n67: - Canonical continuity is contradictory: `spec.md`, `checklist.md`, and `implementation-summary.md` claim completion, while `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `decision-record.md` retai