esis, and save\n\n  Line 90:         on_acquire: \"Capture ownerPid from the JSON output and reuse it for every release below. If acquired=false, stop and present recovery choices — another deep-ai-council run already holds this packet.\"\n\n  Line 92:         # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n\n  Line 94:           action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n\n  Line 139:           - session_result: \"topics_completed, topic_results, skipped_topic_ids, stop_reason\"\n\n  Line 141:   gate_synthesis_approval:\n\n  Line 146:       message: \"Deep council synthesis cancelled; loop artifacts are preserved.\"\n\n  Line 148:   phase_synthesis:\n\n  Line 165:           - stop_reason\n\n  Line 174:       message: \"Deep council save cancelled after synthesis.\"\n\n  Line 180:         action: \"Invoke memory:save routing after synthesis\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-ai-council.body.md:\n  Line 18: capable agent judged itself \"uncertain\" on an abstract question and hard-stopped).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-ai-council-auto.yaml:\n  Line 4: action: Run deep-ai-council session orchestration from setup through synthesis and memory save\n\n  Line 85:         # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n\n  Line 87:           action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n\n  Line 132:           - session_result: \"topics_completed, topic_results, skipped_topic_ids, stop_reason\"\n\n  Line 146:   phase_synthesis:\n\n  Line 163:           - stop_reason\n\n  Line 169:         action: \"Invoke memory:save routing after synthesis\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-command-benchmark-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 124:       step_emit_terminal_envelope:\n\n  Line 125:         action: \"Render the presentation contract's terminal line. STATUS reflects instrumentation only; CONFORMANCE and BEHAVIOR preserve their owners' subject results.\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 23:     and explicitly authorize any promotion. Stops when: operator chooses stop, max iterations reached,\n\n  Line 42:   max_iterations: \"[MAX_ITERATIONS] - Maximum loop iterations before forced stop. Default: 5.\"\n\n  Line 100:     reducer: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs\n\n  Line 142:         command: \"Open {state_paths.lock_file} with exclusive non-blocking advisory locking semantics; if locked, stop and present recovery choices.\"\n\n  Line 143:         note: \"macOS/BSD locking here is advisory. Stale-lock override is confirm-only or explicit recovery-only. Sessions within the same orchestrator process are serialized by design; this guard targets separate terminal invocations racing on the same spec folder.\"\n\n  Line 185:         on_fail: \"Do not present gate_before_candidate. Halt the entire agent-improvement loop (not just this iteration) with STATUS=FAIL: dispatchCaps.maxCandidateDispatches has been reached cumulatively for this session. Emit session_end with stopReason=error, sessionOutcome=advisoryOnly, release the lock, and report the printed cap message verbatim.\"\n\n  Line 226:         on_fail: \"Halt the entire agent-improvement loop (not just this iteration) with STATUS=FAIL: dispatchCaps.maxScoreExecutions has been reached cumulatively for this session. Emit session_end with stopReason=error, sessionOutcome=advisoryOnly, release the lock, and report the printed cap message verbatim.\"\n\n  Line 245:         on_fail: \"Halt the entire agent-improvement loop (not just this iteration) with STATUS=FAIL: dispatchCaps.maxBenchmarkRuns has been reached cumulatively for this session. Emit session_end with stopReason=error, sessionOutcome=advisoryOnly, release the lock, and report the printed cap message verbatim.\"\n\n  Line 255:         on_fail: \"Halt the entire agent-improvement loop (not just this iteration) with STATUS=FAIL: dispatchCaps.maxScoreExecutions has been reached cumulatively for this session. Emit session_end with stopReason=error, sessionOutcome=advisoryOnly, release the lock, and report the printed cap message verbatim.\"\n\n  Line 270:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder}/improvement\"\n\n  Line 280:       step_emit_journal_event_legal_stop_evaluated:\n\n  Line 281:         description: \"Emit legal_stop_evaluated journal event with all five gate bundles after the operator gate is evaluated\"\n\n  Line 282:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs --emit legal_stop_evaluated --journal {spec_folder}/improvement/improvement-journal.jsonl --details '{\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"{session_id}\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":\\\"{iteration}\\\",\\\"gateResults\\\":{\\\"contractGate\\\":\\\"{contract_gate}\\\",\\\"behaviorGate\\\":\\\"{behavior_gate}\\\",\\\"integrationGate\\\":\\\"{integration_gate}\\\",\\\"evidenceGate\\\":\\\"{evidence_gate}\\\",\\\"improvementGate\\\":\\\"{improvement_gate}\\\"},\\\"stopReason\\\":\\\"{stop_reason}\\\"}'\"\n\n  Line 283:       step_emit_journal_event_blocked_stop:\n\n  Line 284:         description: \"Emit blocked_stop when any legal-stop gate fails\"\n\n  Line 286:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs --emit blocked_stop --journal {spec_folder}/improvement/improvement-journal.jsonl --details '{\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"{session_id}\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":\\\"{iteration}\\\",\\\"failedGates\\\":\\\"{failed_gates}\\\",\\\"stopReason\\\":\\\"blockedStop\\\"}'\"\n\n  Line 292:   phase_synthesis:\n\n  Line 296:         description: \"Present final dashboard with per-dimension trends and stop reason\"\n\n  Line 299:         description: \"Recommend continue, promote, or stop based on reducer output\"\n\n  Line 300:         action: \"Check experiment-registry.json for bestPromptRecord and stopStatus\"\n\n  Line 302:         description: \"Emit session_end journal event after synthesis completes\"\n\n  Line 303:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs --emit session_end --journal {spec_folder}/improvement/improvement-journal.jsonl --details '{\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"{session_id}\\\",\\\"stopReason\\\":\\\"{stop_reason}\\\",\\\"sessionOutcome\\\":\\\"{session_outcome}\\\",\\\"endedAt\\\":\\\"{ended_at}\\\",\\\"totalIterations\\\":\\\"{total_iterations}\\\"}'\"\n\n  Line 305:         description: \"Release the advisory lock as the final step of synthesis\"\n\n  Line 307:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"lock_released\",\"path\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"releasePhase\":\"synthesis\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-ai-council-presentation.txt:\n  Line 136:      A) Autonomous - run setup, topic loops, synthesis, and save without approval\n\n  Line 137:      B) Interactive - pause at setup, loop, synthesis, and save gates\n\n  Line 206: purpose: Run iterative multi-topic council sessions until per-topic convergence or cost guards stop the run\n\n  Line 207: action: Execute YAML workflow managing setup, topic loop, synthesis, and save phases\n\n  Line 240: | `:auto` | `/deep:ai-council:auto \"topic\"` | Runs setup, loop, synthesis, and save without approval gates after Tier-1 setup succeeds |\n\n  Line 241: | `:confirm` | `/deep:ai-council:confirm \"topic\"` | Prompts once for setup, then gates setup, loop, synthesis, and save |\n\n  Line 257: - Pauses before setup, loop, synthesis, and save phases.\n\n  Line 283: The YAML contains the full loop workflow: initialization, session orchestration, topic iteration, findings-registry use, synthesis, and memory save.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-alignment.contract.md:\n  Line 100: - DISPATCH ONLY: you dispatch `deep-alignment` to run one iteration; you do NOT read, edit, patch, or run the alignment loop over the target yourself. The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself — setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence checks, synthesis, and all loop-level artifact writes; the `deep-alignment` leaf owns only its own single-iteration artifacts — mixing your own inline work with the dispatch is a route violation.\n\n  Line 103: Your job is to DISPATCH `deep-alignment` to run ONE iteration of the alignment loop over the bound target — NOT to run the loop yourself, and NOT to review, analyze, or summarize this contract. The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself (setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence, synthesis, and loop-level writes). This contract is your instruction set; the alignment target is the bound spec_folder/target named in your message, never this document.\n\n  Line 208: **Convergence policy:** `--coverage-threshold <F>` (default `1.0`) and `--stability-window <N>` (default `2`) tune a two-signal AND-gate. Both must hold together before STOP is legal, and `--max-iterations` remains an independent hard stop regardless. Do NOT transfer `deep-review`'s single `convergenceThreshold` ratio semantics onto these two flags — they are not equivalent.\n\n  Line 370:   - \"{state_paths_config} single terminal status:complete transition only\"\n\n  Line 372:   - \"{state_paths_alignment_output} synthesis write only\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-alignment.body.md:\n  Line 92: `--coverage-threshold <F>` (default `1.0`) and `--stability-window <N>` (default `2`) tune the two-signal AND-gate `deep-alignment/scripts/check-convergence.cjs` evaluates; both must hold together before STOP is legal, and `--max-iterations` remains an independent hard stop regardless of their outcome. Do not transfer `deep-review`'s single `convergenceThreshold` ratio semantics onto these two flags — they are not equivalent.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-model-benchmark-auto.yaml:\n  Line 43:   max_iterations: \"[MAX_ITERATIONS] - Maximum loop iterations before forced stop. Default: 5.\"\n\n  Line 100:     reducer: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs\n\n  Line 136:           action: \"Release {state_paths.lock_file} before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n\n  Line 178:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder}/improvement\"\n\n  Line 179:       step_stop_check:\n\n  Line 180:         description: \"Evaluate stop conditions: score plateau, infra failure, weak aggregate, max iterations\"\n\n  Line 181:         action: \"Stop if experiment-registry.json reports stopStatus.shouldStop: true\"\n\n  Line 182:       step_emit_journal_event_legal_stop_evaluated:\n\n  Line 183:         description: \"Emit legal_stop_evaluated journal event after stop-condition evaluation\"\n\n  Line 184:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs --emit legal_stop_evaluated --journal {spec_folder}/improvement/improvement-journal.jsonl --details '{\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"{session_id}\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":\\\"{iteration}\\\",\\\"scoringMethod\\\":\\\"{scoring_method}\\\",\\\"stopReason\\\":\\\"{stop_reason}\\\"}'\"\n\n  Line 186:   phase_synthesis:\n\n  Line 190:         description: \"Render the final dashboard via reduce-state and present benchmark trends and stop reason\"\n\n  Line 191:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder}/improvement\"\n\n  Line 193:         description: \"Recommend continue, promote, or stop based on reducer output and the benchmark report scoringMethod\"\n\n\n(Results truncated. Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":100,"truncated":true},"title":"reduce-state|synthesis|terminal|stop|maxIterationsReached|resource-map","time":{"start":1784694406323,"end":1784694406353}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_023028bef7535baa016a6046863d40819186d32d3093f11ad3"}},"id":"prt_f88137cad001iqIrJOukdACkME","sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","messageID":"msg_f88134f0e0013UDh1JvAIkhQ2P"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784694406360,"sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ElfQM2hTgcv5u5rpIpxNNT9v","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs","offset":1,"limit":280},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n2: // ║ Deep Review State Reducer                                                ║\n3: // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n4: \n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: // 1. IMPORTS\n9: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: \n11: const fs = require('node:fs');\n12: const path = require('node:path');\n13: const { emitResourceMap } = require('../../shared/synthesis/resource-map.cjs');\n14: const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('../../runtime/lib/deep-loop/artifact-root.cjs');\n15: const { filterCompletionBearingRecords } = require('../../shared/progress/progress-record.cjs');\n16: \n17: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n18: // 2. CONSTANTS\n19: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n20: \n21: const REQUIRED_DIMENSIONS = ['correctness', 'security', 'traceability', 'maintainability'];\n22: const SEVERITY_KEYS = ['P0', 'P1', 'P2'];\n23: const SEVERITY_WEIGHTS = { P0: 10.0, P1: 5.0, P2: 1.0 };\n24: const LIVE_LINEAGE_MODES = new Set(['new', 'resume', 'restart']);\n25: \n26: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n27: // 3. HELPERS\n28: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n29: \n30: function readUtf8(filePath) {\n31:   return fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8');\n32: }\n33: \n34: function writeUtf8(filePath, content) {\n35:   fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(filePath), { recursive: true });\n36:   fs.writeFileSync(filePath, content, 'utf8');\n37: }\n38: \n39: function readJson(filePath) {\n40:   return JSON.parse(readUtf8(filePath));\n41: }\n42: \n43: function getResourceMapEmitSetting(config) {\n44:   const nested = config && typeof config === 'object'\n45:     ? (config.resource_map || config.resourceMap || null)\n46:     : null;\n47:   if (nested && typeof nested === 'object' && typeof nested.emit === 'boolean') {\n48:     return nested.emit;\n49:   }\n50:   return true;\n51: }\n52: \n53: function slugify(value) {\n54:   return value\n55:     .toLowerCase()\n56:     .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')\n57:     .replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '')\n58:     .slice(0, 80) || 'entry';\n59: }\n60: \n61: function normalizeText(value) {\n62:   if (value === null || value === undefined) return '';\n63:   if (typeof value !== 'string') {\n64:     try { return String(value).replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim(); }\n65:     catch { return ''; }\n66:   }\n67:   return value.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n68: }\n69: \n70: function escapeRegExp(value) {\n71:   return value.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&');\n72: }\n73: \n74: function zeroSeverityMap() {\n75:   return { P0: 0, P1: 0, P2: 0 };\n76: }\n77: \n78: function isFiniteNumber(value) {\n79:   return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value);\n80: }\n81: \n82: function normalizeSeverity(value) {\n83:   return SEVERITY_KEYS.includes(value) ? value : null;\n84: }\n85: \n86: function normalizeLineageMode(value) {\n87:   const normalized = normalizeText(value).toLowerCase();\n88:   return LIVE_LINEAGE_MODES.has(normalized) ? normalized : null;\n89: }\n90: \n91: function getNestedField(record, fieldName) {\n92:   if (!record || typeof record !== 'object') {\n93:     return undefined;\n94:   }\n95:   if (record[fieldName] !== undefined) {\n96:     return record[fieldName];\n97:   }\n98:   if (record.details && typeof record.details === 'object' && record.details[fieldName] !== undefined) {\n99:     return record.details[fieldName];\n100:   }\n101:   return undefined;\n102: }\n103: \n104: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n105: // 4. PARSERS\n106: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n107: \n108: /**\n109:  * Parse JSONL content into an array of records, preserving both iteration and\n110:  * event rows. Backward-compatible array return.\n111:  *\n112:  * @param {string} jsonlContent - Newline-delimited JSON string\n113:  * @returns {Array<Object>} Parsed records (corrupt lines silently dropped — use parseJsonlDetailed for fail-closed behavior)\n114:  */\n115: function parseJsonl(jsonlContent) {\n116:   return parseJsonlDetailed(jsonlContent).records;\n117: }\n118: \n119: /**\n120:  * Parse JSONL content and report malformed lines (fail-closed pathway).\n121:  *\n122:  * Returns both the parsed records and a corruption warning list. The reducer\n123:  * exit code is non-zero when warnings are present unless `--lenient` is passed.\n124:  *\n125:  * @param {string} jsonlContent - Newline-delimited JSON string\n126:  * @returns {{records: Array<Object>, corruptionWarnings: Array<{line: number, raw: string, error: string}>}}\n127:  */\n128: function parseJsonlDetailed(jsonlContent) {\n129:   const records = [];\n130:   const corruptionWarnings = [];\n131:   let lineNumber = 0;\n132: \n133:   for (const rawLine of jsonlContent.split('\\n')) {\n134:     lineNumber += 1;\n135:     const line = rawLine.trim();\n136:     if (!line) {\n137:       continue;\n138:     }\n139: \n140:     try {\n141:       records.push(JSON.parse(line));\n142:     } catch (error) {\n143:       corruptionWarnings.push({\n144:         line: lineNumber,\n145:         raw: rawLine.length > 200 ? `${rawLine.slice(0, 200)}...` : rawLine,\n146:         error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n147:       });\n148:     }\n149:   }\n150: \n151:   return { records, corruptionWarnings };\n152: }\n153: \n154: function loadDeltaPayloads(deltaDir) {\n155:   if (!fs.existsSync(deltaDir)) {\n156:     return [];\n157:   }\n158: \n159:   return fs.readdirSync(deltaDir)\n160:     .filter((fileName) => /^iter-\\d+\\.jsonl$/.test(fileName))\n161:     .sort((left, right) => left.localeCompare(right, undefined, { numeric: true }))\n162:     .map((fileName) => {\n163:       const { records, corruptionWarnings } = parseJsonlDetailed(readUtf8(path.join(deltaDir, fileName)));\n164:       if (!corruptionWarnings.length) {\n165:         return records;\n166:       }\n167:       console.warn(\n168:         `[deep-review] resource-map extractor skipped ${corruptionWarnings.length} malformed delta row(s) from ${fileName}`,\n169:       );\n170:       return records.concat(new Array(corruptionWarnings.length).fill(null));\n171:     });\n172: }\n173: \n174: function extractSection(markdown, heading) {\n175:   const pattern = new RegExp(`(?:^|\\\\n)##\\\\s+${escapeRegExp(heading)}\\\\s*\\\\n([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)(?=\\\\n##\\\\s|$)`, 'i');\n176:   const match = markdown.match(pattern);\n177:   return match ? match[1].trim() : '';\n178: }\n179: \n180: function extractSubsection(sectionText, subheading) {\n181:   const pattern = new RegExp(`(?:^|\\\\n)###\\\\s+${escapeRegExp(subheading)}[^\\\\n]*\\\\n([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)(?=\\\\n###\\\\s|\\\\n##\\\\s|$)`, 'i');\n182:   const match = sectionText.match(pattern);\n183:   return match ? match[1].trim() : '';\n184: }\n185: \n186: function extractListItems(sectionText) {\n187:   return sectionText\n188:     .split('\\n')\n189:     .map((line) => line.trim())\n190:     .filter((line) => /^([-*]|\\d+\\.)\\s+/.test(line))\n191:     .map((line) => normalizeText(line.replace(/^([-*]|\\d+\\.)\\s+/, '')))\n192:     .filter(Boolean);\n193: }\n194: \n195: /**\n196:  * Parse a finding line of the form: `- **F001**: Title — file:line — Description`\n197:  *\n198:  * @param {string} line - Raw finding bullet\n199:  * @param {string} severity - P0, P1, or P2 context\n200:  * @returns {Object|null} Structured finding or null when the line is not a finding\n201:  */\n202: function parseFindingLine(line, severity) {\n203:   const match = line.match(/^\\*\\*(F\\d+)\\*\\*\\s*:\\s*(.+?)(?:\\s+[—-]\\s+`?([^`]+?)`?)?(?:\\s+[—-]\\s+(.+))?$/);\n204:   if (!match) {\n205:     return null;\n206:   }\n207: \n208:   const [, findingId, title, evidenceRaw, description] = match;\n209:   let file = null;\n210:   let lineNumber = null;\n211: \n212:   if (evidenceRaw) {\n213:     const evidenceMatch = evidenceRaw.trim().match(/^(.+?):(\\d+)(?:[:-].*)?$/);\n214:     if (evidenceMatch) {\n215:       file = evidenceMatch[1];\n216:       lineNumber = Number(evidenceMatch[2]);\n217:     } else {\n218:       file = evidenceRaw.trim();\n219:     }\n220:   }\n221: \n222:   return {\n223:     findingId,\n224:     severity,\n225:     title: normalizeText(title),\n226:     file,\n227:     line: lineNumber,\n228:     description: normalizeText(description || ''),\n229:   };\n230: }\n231: \n232: function parseFindingsBlock(sectionText, severity) {\n233:   if (!sectionText) {\n234:     return [];\n235:   }\n236: \n237:   return sectionText\n238:     .split('\\n')\n239:     .map((line) => line.trim())\n240:     .filter((line) => /^-\\s+\\*\\*F\\d+\\*\\*/.test(line))\n241:     .map((line) => parseFindingLine(line.replace(/^-\\s+/, ''), severity))\n242:     .filter(Boolean);\n243: }\n244: \n245: /**\n246:  * Parse a single iteration markdown file into a structured review record.\n247:  *\n248:  * @param {string} iterationPath - Absolute path to an iteration-NNN.md file\n249:  * @returns {Object} Parsed iteration with focus, findings, cross-reference, and reflection fields\n250:  */\n251: function parseIterationFile(iterationPath) {\n252:   const markdown = readUtf8(iterationPath);\n253:   const runMatch = iterationPath.match(/iteration-(\\d+)\\.md$/);\n254:   const headingMatch = markdown.match(/^#\\s+Iteration\\s+\\d+\\s*[-:]\\s+(.+)$/m);\n255: \n256:   // Support both old schema (Focus/Findings/Ruled Out/Dead Ends/Assessment)\n257:   // and live schema (Dispatcher/Files Reviewed/Findings - New/Traceability Checks/\n258:   // Confirmed-Clean/Next Focus).\n259:   const focusSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Focus') || extractSection(markdown, 'Dispatcher');\n260:   const findingsSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Findings') || extractSection(markdown, 'Findings - New');\n261:   const ruledOutSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Ruled Out') || extractSection(markdown, 'Confirmed-Clean Surfaces') || extractSection(markdown, 'Confirmed-Clean');\n262:   const deadEndsSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Dead Ends') || extractSection(markdown, 'Traceability Checks');\n263:   const nextFocusSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Recommended Next Focus') || extractSection(markdown, 'Next Focus (recommendation)') || extractSection(markdown, 'Next Focus');\n264:   const assessmentSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Assessment');\n265:   const filesReviewedSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Files Reviewed');\n266: \n267:   const p0Block = extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P0') || extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P0 Findings');\n268:   const p1Block = extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P1') || extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P1 Findings');\n269:   const p2Block = extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P2') || extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P2 Findings');\n270: \n271:   const findings = [\n272:     ...parseFindingsBlock(p0Block, 'P0'),\n273:     ...parseFindingsBlock(p1Block, 'P1'),\n274:     ...parseFindingsBlock(p2Block, 'P2'),\n275:   ];\n276: \n277:   const dimensionsAddressed = (assessmentSection.match(/Dimensions addressed:\\s*(.+)/i) || [])[1];\n278: \n279:   return {\n280:     path: iterationPath,\n\n(Showing lines 1-280 of 2253. Use offset=281 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n// ║ Deep Review State Reducer                                                ║\n// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n\n'use strict';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst fs = require('node:fs');\nconst path = require('node:path');\nconst { emitResourceMap } = require('../../shared/synthesis/resource-map.cjs');\nconst { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('../../runtime/lib/deep-loop/artifact-root.cjs');\nconst { filterCompletionBearingRecords } = require('../../shared/progress/progress-record.cjs');\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs","text":"// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n// ║ Deep Review State Reducer                                                ║\n// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n\n'use strict';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst fs = require('node:fs');\nconst path = require('node:path');\nconst { emitResourceMap } = require('../../shared/synthesis/resource-map.cjs');\nconst { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('../../runtime/lib/deep-loop/artifact-root.cjs');\nconst { filterCompletionBearingRecords } = require('../../shared/progress/progress-record.cjs');\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst REQUIRED_DIMENSIONS = ['correctness', 'security', 'traceability', 'maintainability'];\nconst SEVERITY_KEYS = ['P0', 'P1', 'P2'];\nconst SEVERITY_WEIGHTS = { P0: 10.0, P1: 5.0, P2: 1.0 };\nconst LIVE_LINEAGE_MODES = new Set(['new', 'resume', 'restart']);\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. HELPERS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfunction readUtf8(filePath) {\n  return fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8');\n}\n\nfunction writeUtf8(filePath, content) {\n  fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(filePath), { recursive: true });\n  fs.writeFileSync(filePath, content, 'utf8');\n}\n\nfunction readJson(filePath) {\n  return JSON.parse(readUtf8(filePath));\n}\n\nfunction getResourceMapEmitSetting(config) {\n  const nested = config && typeof config === 'object'\n    ? (config.resource_map || config.resourceMap || null)\n    : null;\n  if (nested && typeof nested === 'object' && typeof nested.emit === 'boolean') {\n    return nested.emit;\n  }\n  return true;\n}\n\nfunction slugify(value) {\n  return value\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')\n    .replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '')\n    .slice(0, 80) || 'entry';\n}\n\nfunction normalizeText(value) {\n  if (value === null || value === undefined) return '';\n  if (typeof value !== 'string') {\n    try { return String(value).replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim(); }\n    catch { return ''; }\n  }\n  return value.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n}\n\nfunction escapeRegExp(value) {\n  return value.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&');\n}\n\nfunction zeroSeverityMap() {\n  return { P0: 0, P1: 0, P2: 0 };\n}\n\nfunction isFiniteNumber(value) {\n  return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value);\n}\n\nfunction normalizeSeverity(value) {\n  return SEVERITY_KEYS.includes(value) ? value : null;\n}\n\nfunction normalizeLineageMode(value) {\n  const normalized = normalizeText(value).toLowerCase();\n  return LIVE_LINEAGE_MODES.has(normalized) ? normalized : null;\n}\n\nfunction getNestedField(record, fieldName) {\n  if (!record || typeof record !== 'object') {\n    return undefined;\n  }\n  if (record[fieldName] !== undefined) {\n    return record[fieldName];\n  }\n  if (record.details && typeof record.details === 'object' && record.details[fieldName] !== undefined) {\n    return record.details[fieldName];\n  }\n  return undefined;\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. PARSERS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/**\n * Parse JSONL content into an array of records, preserving both iteration and\n * event rows. Backward-compatible array return.\n *\n * @param {string} jsonlContent - Newline-delimited JSON string\n * @returns {Array<Object>} Parsed records (corrupt lines silently dropped — use parseJsonlDetailed for fail-closed behavior)\n */\nfunction parseJsonl(jsonlContent) {\n  return parseJsonlDetailed(jsonlContent).records;\n}\n\n/**\n * Parse JSONL content and report malformed lines (fail-closed pathway).\n *\n * Returns both the parsed records and a corruption warning list. The reducer\n * exit code is non-zero when warnings are present unless `--lenient` is passed.\n *\n * @param {string} jsonlContent - Newline-delimited JSON string\n * @returns {{records: Array<Object>, corruptionWarnings: Array<{line: number, raw: string, error: string}>}}\n */\nfunction parseJsonlDetailed(jsonlContent) {\n  const records = [];\n  const corruptionWarnings = [];\n  let lineNumber = 0;\n\n  for (const rawLine of jsonlContent.split('\\n')) {\n    lineNumber += 1;\n    const line = rawLine.trim();\n    if (!line) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    try {\n      records.push(JSON.parse(line));\n    } catch (error) {\n      corruptionWarnings.push({\n        line: lineNumber,\n        raw: rawLine.length > 200 ? `${rawLine.slice(0, 200)}...` : rawLine,\n        error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  return { records, corruptionWarnings };\n}\n\nfunction loadDeltaPayloads(deltaDir) {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(deltaDir)) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  return fs.readdirSync(deltaDir)\n    .filter((fileName) => /^iter-\\d+\\.jsonl$/.test(fileName))\n    .sort((left, right) => left.localeCompare(right, undefined, { numeric: true }))\n    .map((fileName) => {\n      const { records, corruptionWarnings } = parseJsonlDetailed(readUtf8(path.join(deltaDir, fileName)));\n      if (!corruptionWarnings.length) {\n        return records;\n      }\n      console.warn(\n        `[deep-review] resource-map extractor skipped ${corruptionWarnings.length} malformed delta row(s) from ${fileName}`,\n      );\n      return records.concat(new Array(corruptionWarnings.length).fill(null));\n    });\n}\n\nfunction extractSection(markdown, heading) {\n  const pattern = new RegExp(`(?:^|\\\\n)##\\\\s+${escapeRegExp(heading)}\\\\s*\\\\n([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)(?=\\\\n##\\\\s|$)`, 'i');\n  const match = markdown.match(pattern);\n  return match ? match[1].trim() : '';\n}\n\nfunction extractSubsection(sectionText, subheading) {\n  const pattern = new RegExp(`(?:^|\\\\n)###\\\\s+${escapeRegExp(subheading)}[^\\\\n]*\\\\n([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)(?=\\\\n###\\\\s|\\\\n##\\\\s|$)`, 'i');\n  const match = sectionText.match(pattern);\n  return match ? match[1].trim() : '';\n}\n\nfunction extractListItems(sectionText) {\n  return sectionText\n    .split('\\n')\n    .map((line) => line.trim())\n    .filter((line) => /^([-*]|\\d+\\.)\\s+/.test(line))\n    .map((line) => normalizeText(line.replace(/^([-*]|\\d+\\.)\\s+/, '')))\n    .filter(Boolean);\n}\n\n/**\n * Parse a finding line of the form: `- **F001**: Title — file:line — Description`\n *\n * @param {string} line - Raw finding bullet\n * @param {string} severity - P0, P1, or P2 context\n * @returns {Object|null} Structured finding or null when the line is not a finding\n */\nfunction parseFindingLine(line, severity) {\n  const match = line.match(/^\\*\\*(F\\d+)\\*\\*\\s*:\\s*(.+?)(?:\\s+[—-]\\s+`?([^`]+?)`?)?(?:\\s+[—-]\\s+(.+))?$/);\n  if (!match) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  const [, findingId, title, evidenceRaw, description] = match;\n  let file = null;\n  let lineNumber = null;\n\n  if (evidenceRaw) {\n    const evidenceMatch = evidenceRaw.trim().match(/^(.+?):(\\d+)(?:[:-].*)?$/);\n    if (evidenceMatch) {\n      file = evidenceMatch[1];\n      lineNumber = Number(evidenceMatch[2]);\n    } else {\n      file = evidenceRaw.trim();\n    }\n  }\n\n  return {\n    findingId,\n    severity,\n    title: normalizeText(title),\n    file,\n    line: lineNumber,\n    description: normalizeText(description || ''),\n  };\n}\n\nfunction parseFindingsBlock(sectionText, severity) {\n  if (!sectionText) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  return sectionText\n    .split('\\n')\n    .map((line) => line.trim())\n    .filter((line) => /^-\\s+\\*\\*F\\d+\\*\\*/.test(line))\n    .map((line) => parseFindingLine(line.replace(/^-\\s+/, ''), severity))\n    .filter(Boolean);\n}\n\n/**\n * Parse a single iteration markdown file into a structured review record.\n *\n * @param {string} iterationPath - Absolute path to an iteration-NNN.md file\n * @returns {Object} Parsed iteration with focus, findings, cross-reference, and reflection fields\n */\nfunction parseIterationFile(iterationPath) {\n  const markdown = readUtf8(iterationPath);\n  const runMatch = iterationPath.match(/iteration-(\\d+)\\.md$/);\n  const headingMatch = markdown.match(/^#\\s+Iteration\\s+\\d+\\s*[-:]\\s+(.+)$/m);\n\n  // Support both old schema (Focus/Findings/Ruled Out/Dead Ends/Assessment)\n  // and live schema (Dispatcher/Files Reviewed/Findings - New/Traceability Checks/\n  // Confirmed-Clean/Next Focus).\n  const focusSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Focus') || extractSection(markdown, 'Dispatcher');\n  const findingsSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Findings') || extractSection(markdown, 'Findings - New');\n  const ruledOutSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Ruled Out') || extractSection(markdown, 'Confirmed-Clean Surfaces') || extractSection(markdown, 'Confirmed-Clean');\n  const deadEndsSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Dead Ends') || extractSection(markdown, 'Traceability Checks');\n  const nextFocusSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Recommended Next Focus') || extractSection(markdown, 'Next Focus (recommendation)') || extractSection(markdown, 'Next Focus');\n  const assessmentSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Assessment');\n  const filesReviewedSection = extractSection(markdown, 'Files Reviewed');\n\n  const p0Block = extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P0') || extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P0 Findings');\n  const p1Block = extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P1') || extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P1 Findings');\n  const p2Block = extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P2') || extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P2 Findings');\n\n  const findings = [\n    ...parseFindingsBlock(p0Block, 'P0'),\n    ...parseFindingsBlock(p1Block, 'P1'),\n    ...parseFindingsBlock(p2Block, 'P2'),\n  ];\n\n  const dimensionsAddressed = (assessmentSection.match(/Dimensions addressed:\\s*(.+)/i) || [])[1];\n\n  return {\n    path: iterationPath,","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":280,"totalLines":2253,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs","time":{"start":1784694406314,"end":1784694406356}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_023028bef7535baa016a6046863d388191bf7bbe961c3e3e2c"}},"id":"prt_f88137ca50015Q50gqn5qdJZNu","sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","messageID":"msg_f88134f0e0013UDh1JvAIkhQ2P"}}
