{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1784694654489,"sessionID":"ses_07813ae5affewXVPxSkMs6ShHp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_lfrFkWKrAyE5GRioQQ4T2G4G","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/review/lineages/sol-high/deep-review-findings-registry.json","offset":1,"limit":190},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/review/lineages/sol-high/deep-review-findings-registry.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"sessionId\": \"fanout-sol-high-1784691838667-iv78vk\",\n3:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n4:   \"generation\": 1,\n5:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n6:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n7:   \"terminalStop\": null,\n8:   \"status\": \"INITIALIZED\",\n9:   \"openFindings\": [\n10:     {\n11:       \"findingId\": \"F001\",\n12:       \"severity\": \"P1\",\n13:       \"title\": \"Refresh can overwrite a concurrent serving-state update\",\n14:       \"file\": \".opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs\",\n15:       \"line\": 550,\n16:       \"description\": \"The function reads and validates the existing manifest, caches `servingAuthority` and `shadowOnly`, performs compilation, then writes unconditionally. A concurrent writer that changes either serving field after line 552 but before line 588 is silently reverted by stale cached values. The mint path has an explicit concurrent-writer test, while refresh has no lock, compare-and-swap, fingerprint recheck, or concurrency test. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:550-590] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs:457-472] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs:501-605]\",\n17:       \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n18:       \"firstSeen\": 1,\n19:       \"lastSeen\": 1,\n20:       \"status\": \"active\",\n21:       \"transitions\": [\n22:         {\n23:           \"iteration\": 1,\n24:           \"from\": null,\n25:           \"to\": \"P1\",\n26:           \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\"\n27:         }\n28:       ],\n29:       \"dimensions\": [\n30:         \"correctness\"\n31:       ],\n32:       \"mergedFindingIds\": []\n33:     },\n34:     {\n35:       \"findingId\": \"F002\",\n36:       \"severity\": \"P1\",\n37:       \"title\": \"Cutover gate false-passes compiled `clarify` and `reject` decisions\",\n38:       \"file\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/skill-benchmark/cutover-playbook-executor.cjs\",\n39:       \"line\": 207,\n40:       \"description\": \"The gate labels any decision whose action is not `route` as `compiled-defers-to-legacy` and returns PASS. Compiled routers actually emit `clarify` and `reject`; those are terminal decisions, not legacy fallback. A compiled reject or clarify that disagrees with a legacy route therefore bypasses intent comparison and false-passes the cutover gate. The test suite covers only explicit `defer`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/skill-benchmark/cutover-playbook-executor.cjs:207-217] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/skill-benchmark/tests/compiled-routing-cutover-luna.test.cjs:62-70] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/006-parent-hub-rollout/004-cli-external-orchestration/lib/router.cjs:40-66] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/006-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/router.cjs:140-153]\",\n41:       \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n42:       \"firstSeen\": 2,\n43:       \"lastSeen\": 2,\n44:       \"status\": \"active\",\n45:       \"transitions\": [\n46:         {\n47:           \"iteration\": 2,\n48:           \"from\": null,\n49:           \"to\": \"P1\",\n50:           \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\"\n51:         }\n52:       ],\n53:       \"dimensions\": [\n54:         \"correctness\"\n55:       ],\n56:       \"mergedFindingIds\": []\n57:     },\n58:     {\n59:       \"findingId\": \"F003\",\n60:       \"severity\": \"P1\",\n61:       \"title\": \"Packet claims completion while its own required completion gates remain open\",\n62:       \"file\": \".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md\",\n63:       \"line\": 52,\n64:       \"description\": \"The protocol says P1 items must complete or receive user approval, but P1 items CHK-025, CHK-040, CHK-041, and CHK-140 remain unchecked, and formal operator sign-off is blank. At the same time, the checklist and spec declare `complete`; `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `decision-record.md` retain `planned` frontmatter, unchecked definition-of-done/tasks, and stale blockers. No approval evidence resolves the contradiction. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:52-58] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:92-92] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:123-124] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:142-148] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/checklist.md:197-208] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/plan.md:11-11] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/tasks.md:10-19] ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n65:       \"dimension\": \"traceability\",\n66:       \"firstSeen\": 4,\n67:       \"lastSeen\": 4,\n68:       \"status\": \"active\",\n69:       \"transitions\": [\n70:         {\n71:           \"iteration\": 4,\n72:           \"from\": null,\n73:           \"to\": \"P1\",\n74:           \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\"\n75:         }\n76:       ],\n77:       \"dimensions\": [\n78:         \"traceability\"\n79:       ],\n80:       \"mergedFindingIds\": []\n81:     },\n82:     {\n83:       \"findingId\": \"F005\",\n84:       \"severity\": \"P1\",\n85:       \"title\": \"`sk-doc` compiled matcher over-routes `preview` as `review`\",\n86:       \"file\": \".opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/006-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/router.cjs\",\n87:       \"line\": 23,\n88:       \"description\": \"The compiled router substring-matches every non-command keyword. `sk-doc`'s quality vocabulary contains bare `review`, while the frozen legacy replay applies a word boundary specifically so `preview` does not match `review`. Direct replay confirms the divergence: compiled routes `\\\"preview this document\\\"` to `create-quality-control`; legacy returns no intents and `deferReason: no-mode-scored`. This disproves byte-identical behavior beyond the finite route-gold corpus. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/006-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/router.cjs:23-29] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/006-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/router.cjs:174-184] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json:37] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/skill-benchmark/router-replay.cjs:440-453]\",\n89:       \"dimension\": \"maintainability\",\n90:       \"firstSeen\": 5,\n91:       \"lastSeen\": 6,\n92:       \"status\": \"active\",\n93:       \"transitions\": [\n94:         {\n95:           \"iteration\": 5,\n96:           \"from\": null,\n97:           \"to\": \"P1\",\n98:           \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\"\n99:         }\n100:       ],\n101:       \"dimensions\": [\n102:         \"maintainability\"\n103:       ],\n104:       \"mergedFindingIds\": []\n105:     },\n106:     {\n107:       \"findingId\": \"F007\",\n108:       \"severity\": \"P1\",\n109:       \"title\": \"Current manifest suite fails its authored-closure sync assertion\",\n110:       \"file\": \".opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs\",\n111:       \"line\": 378,\n112:       \"description\": \"Live execution of `node --test .opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs` passed 15/16 and failed the sync capture/restore test. `compiled-route-sync.cjs --check` reports `UNRESOLVED: sk-code, system-deep-loop, mcp-tooling, sk-doc`, so the assertion that all seven authored hubs resolve no longer holds. This contradicts the packet's green-suite evidence and blocks a completion claim even though promoted runtime status is currently fresh. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs:378-411] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs:351-357]\",\n113:       \"dimension\": \"traceability\",\n114:       \"firstSeen\": 7,\n115:       \"lastSeen\": 8,\n116:       \"status\": \"active\",\n117:       \"transitions\": [\n118:         {\n119:           \"iteration\": 7,\n120:           \"from\": null,\n121:           \"to\": \"P1\",\n122:           \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\"\n123:         }\n124:       ],\n125:       \"dimensions\": [\n126:         \"traceability\"\n127:       ],\n128:       \"mergedFindingIds\": []\n129:     },\n130:     {\n131:       \"findingId\": \"F004\",\n132:       \"severity\": \"P2\",\n133:       \"title\": \"SD-015 test limitation is stale\",\n134:       \"file\": \".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/implementation-summary.md\",\n135:       \"line\": 204,\n136:       \"description\": \"The summary says there is no dedicated SD-015 lock-in test and leaves the follow-up unchecked, but `compiled-routing-parity.vitest.ts` contains a named SD-015 positive test plus a negative route-gap twin. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-sk-doc-router-alignment/020-router-unification-program/007-unified-refactor-implementation/015-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/implementation-summary.md:204-220] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/skill-benchmark/tests/compiled-routing-parity.vitest.ts:468-534]\",\n137:       \"dimension\": \"traceability\",\n138:       \"firstSeen\": 4,\n139:       \"lastSeen\": 4,\n140:       \"status\": \"active\",\n141:       \"transitions\": [\n142:         {\n143:           \"iteration\": 4,\n144:           \"from\": null,\n145:           \"to\": \"P2\",\n146:           \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\"\n147:         }\n148:       ],\n149:       \"dimensions\": [\n150:         \"traceability\"\n151:       ],\n152:       \"mergedFindingIds\": []\n153:     },\n154:     {\n155:       \"findingId\": \"F